<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39712" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pū^tresco</span></b>  (not in Cic.; for in Tusc. 1,
		3, putescat is the correct read.), ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i> [putreo].
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To grow rotten</i> or <i>putrid</i>,
				<i>to rot</i>, <i>putrefy</i>, <i>moulder</i>, <i>decay</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne ungulae putrescant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestis putrescit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 3, 119</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 9, 45, § 101</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 3, 25, 15</span></i>
			: medullae, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 4,
			131: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cicatrices,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 37, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To become loose</i> or <i>friable</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 2, 11, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 11, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 2, 61</span></i>; 11, 3,
			56.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to fall into
			contempt</i>, <i>become disgusting</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et nomen impiorum putrescet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Prov. 10, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				Jer. 13, 9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
